    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d387">

                <pb facs="0457" n="447" sameAs="frus:frus1948v08/pg447"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.50 Recovery/1–548</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Chief of the Division of Chinese
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Ringwalt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Director of the Office of Far Eastern Affairs</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Butterworth</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-01-05">January 5, 1948</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Attached is a statement prepared by Mr. Magill<anchor n="13" xml:id="d387-f1"/>
                    setting forth what I understand to be the FE<anchor n="14" xml:id="d387-f2"/>
                    position on issues involved in formulation of the China Aid Program. It occurs
                    to me that it might be useful in any decision that is being reached by the
                    Secretary. We <pb facs="0458" n="448" xml:id="pg448"/> stand ready to put it in
                    any form you think necessary. In any case, it furnishes a record of FE’s
                    views.</p>
                <closer><signed>A[<hi rendition="#small-caps">rthur</hi>] R. R[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ingwalt</hi>]</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d387-a1.xml" xpointer="d387-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d387-f1" n="13" xml:id="d387-f1-content">
                <p>Robert N. Magill, of the Division of Chinese Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d387-f2" n="14" xml:id="d387-f2-content">
